SHATTERED DIMENSIONS - FREEWARE LICENCE (version 1.0)

DRAFT FOR LEGAL REVIEW. This text was written by the project team, not by a lawyer.

Copyright (c) 2026 The Shattered Dimensions team. All rights reserved.

Shattered Dimensions ("the Software") is the release download made by the Shattered Dimensions team: the setup
program, the translator, the engine and the other files we wrote, and the game the setup builds from them on your
computer. Files from other people that come with the Software are listed under "Other people's work" below.

1. WHAT YOU MAY DO

   You may download the Software free of charge and install and use it on your own computers, for your own
   personal, non-commercial use.

   You may make texture packs and other modifications through the formats we document (the texture pack guide),
   and share your own work. You keep the rights to what you create. Sharing must not include any of the Software's
   own files or anything from the game listed in section 3.

2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

   Unless the Shattered Dimensions team allows it in writing, you may not:
   a. sell, rent or charge for the Software, or include it in anything that is sold;
   b. share, re-host or redistribute the Software or any part of it, changed or unchanged. Point people to the
      official download instead (the Shattered Dimensions website and its GitHub release page). This protects
      players: only official copies are signed and receive updates;
   c. remove or change this licence, the credits or the notices that come with the Software;
   d. present the Software, or a changed copy, as your own work.

   Section 2 does not limit any right that the law gives you and that cannot be taken away by a licence.

3. THE GAME IS YOURS TO SUPPLY

   The Software contains no game data and no game code. It works only with a decrypted copy of your own cartridge
   of The Legend of Zelda: A Link Between Worlds (USA), which you must obtain lawfully. Never distribute the Software
   together with any game files, keys or anything taken from the game, and never use it with a copy you do not own.

4. WHAT IS OURS AND WHAT IS NOT

   Everything in the Software was made by the Shattered Dimensions team and belongs to us, except the files listed
   under "Other people's work" below. This includes the engine, the setup program, the translator, the tools, the
   interface, and all of the Software's artwork and text, its icon artwork included.

   The only thing that is not ours is the game: The Legend of Zelda: A Link Between Worlds, with its code, data,
   music and art, and its characters, names and symbols (among them Link and the Triforce), wherever they appear,
   including in our own artwork. These belong to Nintendo. The Software contains none of the game's files; you supply
   the game yourself (section 3).

5. NOT AFFILIATED WITH NINTENDO

   Shattered Dimensions is an unofficial project. It is not made, endorsed or supported by Nintendo or any company
   connected with it. Nintendo, The Legend of Zelda and A Link Between Worlds are trademarks of their owners and are
   named only to say which game the Software works with, and appear in our artwork as fan art of that game.

6. OTHER PEOPLE'S WORK

   Some files that come with the Software belong to others and are provided under their own licences, which this
   licence does not change: among them Dear ImGui, CityHash, stb, the compiler toolchain from MSYS2 (GCC and binutils
   under the GNU GPL, with the source available as described in TOOLCHAIN.txt), NVIDIA Streamline, the upscaling
   models, the fonts and the textures. Their licences and notices are in the licenses folder. Our thanks go to World
   Across by PaceTea, whose research helped this project, as the credits describe.

7. NO WARRANTY

   The Software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including fitness for a
   particular purpose. Back up your saves. To the extent the law allows, the Shattered Dimensions team is not liable
   for any damage or loss arising from the Software or its use.

8. ENDING

   This licence ends automatically if you break it. You must then stop using the Software and delete your copies.

9. CHANGES

   Later versions of the Software may come with a newer version of this licence, which then applies to them.

